#uuid "3cb1f592-094a-5b91-bac8-80971fe96ac3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392442}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bde0cdd0-7dbe-5ba4-9b36-e66cfe099501" :question/math-academy-id "q-41949" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ is the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $1$st *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+3.5\\cdot 0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1+2\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 0+(-2.5)\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be5f5e04-2f01-53f2-8591-c58133cd71f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099610} {:answer/id #uuid "cea56a00-7b9a-582e-bb36-014f084a08d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099611} {:answer/id #uuid "19e549cb-f70f-5feb-a295-b0871f09f0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3.2 \\\\ 1\\end{bma