y the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\cdot C \\\\  & =C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6afbb954-8251-54c6-9289-3b7b67977c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485049} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8c7b20-ab9a-5f82-aa71-ab274f566e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485162} {:answer/id #uuid "a457aec9-c905-57bd-a32b-334aab799f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485175} {:answer/id #uuid "d93c949b-2601-5a6c-bdfe-2a018e7d7553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -\\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485273} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1e4f5-2794-5ee2-870f-276a9e8a1fc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6afbb954-8251-54c6-9289-3b7b67977c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485049} :answer-field/id #uuid "1201651f-fb8b-5f4f-9fec-edb4aa86cc4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485374}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72e0b567-7c07-513e-b4b8-2088d6f698dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-75612" :question/problem "Find $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & =3{I}_{3}C \\\\  & =3C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115057 :question/id #uuid "3b1395b6-49c1-5e0d-ac94-c2d6fc242f6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4412" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n![](images/32/32c0a3389207452c52376ce4305109e1c5ed634a07d2c99771825c39b5482940.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aebb4360-8326-58cc-a7ca-816d512eec3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113906} {:answer/id #uuid "ef45baf8-81df-5edc-9d1e-1ffb3358dcbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113907} {:answer/id #uuid "fc44e8aa-6f75-5291-a8dc-77e56b4a3328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113908} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6a475f-9fef-5ea6-9665-a0ab5dbd5770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113909} {:answer/id #uuid "6a24c934-0494-5b2e-aa71-129d78fcdbcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113910}] :answer-field/id #uuid "969084eb-bca2-5ea0-bef4-60a97533d6d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "334cfb64-857e-505a-9a43-d21f8e1caef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392430} {:answer/id #uuid "aad0983e-16d3-5538-b3b8-9b0e2aff415b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392431} {:answer/id #uuid "83c87507-4794-5dbb-9918-43c4f3143e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392432} {:answer/id #uuid "6010500b-541c-5b97-806c-4f018455b4cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392433} {:answer/id #uuid "5816752b-1281-5b14-8078-9753e15cfdd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5816752b-1281-5b14-8078-9753e15cfdd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392434} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a0ff826-a7be-5da5-888c-b90181819cf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392429}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d05ca169-7c67-546f-9f08-0fce1486794c" :question/math-academy-id "q-41785" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c24ee771-dbe8-598f-84ff-60f041661edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113948} {:answer/id #uuid "31f22e55-3257-560c-9b8b-1a370672646f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113949} {:answer/id #uuid "41fb8df9-f182-543a-ad39-bd4d9406f6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113950} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8e5b8a-9724-51db-b122-6afd0420a1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113951} {:answer/id #uuid "63361cf3-7b7e-5c0a-8a4d-0ce1232f5d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113952}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9e1c3b65-2a4d-5f95-b0da-0c05529f3648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113947}] :question/id #uuid "7171223c-0a20-5fbc-a656-b17651c3059d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42257" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19780864-9003-505a-b598-f3378103858e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263242} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6518a0-5e35-59b6-b899-07522f46b179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -7 & -21 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263268} {:answer/id #uuid "5517ab5e-f687-5ce4-852d-48dfec575a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263733} {:answer/id #uuid "55a69114-638a-51d0-954d-1a1fa82cd27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -9 & 24 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263735} {:answer/id #uuid "ce129b66-be90-56f8-b1fe-b394c797c064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce129b66-be90-56f8-b1fe-b394c797c064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264802} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ab1d01-3d95-5a64-a3f9-0807a0efbbe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265368}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e430effe-7959-580a-be3d-d4b5f50f0d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-130313" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62b9489d-1bd9-53ad-9584-412222a7fecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62b9489d-1bd9-53ad-9584-412222a7fecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291053} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a8b6a87-5f6a-54ec-bbe9-05756798dc46" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291835} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13580f