} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 11 \\\\ -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd518271-b6ed-5c19-b1f0-393f5d4b8f36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd518271-b6ed-5c19-b1f0-393f5d4b8f36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298377} :answer-field/id #uuid "09562407-6377-5f46-b640-be889d264ee7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b65fdb3-261f-58f4-bc52-fe28b1a030a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b65fdb3-261f-58f4-bc52-fe28b1a030a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297937} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b6da1c0-a6b2-5ebf-9ab8-b2f3c505f543" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answ