ltiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4caef308-f829-5678-91b0-8c356246d3db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408051} {:answer/id #uuid "5305f733-f1f5-5fee-a5d0-db365d37810d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408052} {:answer/id #uuid "adb0e76d-9986-5b8e-a736-d4821798cae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408058} {:answer/id #uuid "efb8a5b6-21b1-5345-9b9e-e436922d4029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408063} {:answer/id #uuid "feae4636-ed31-53a4-b5a1-dfde035b20cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feae4636-ed31-53a4-b5a1-dfde035b20cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408064} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb9eed7-da79-5b44-8508-0e1881d8523f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408066}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38a55885-c791-5e66-b4d4-e155d750a7c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130322" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c8bceae-a8f8-59df-9913-53898f44b673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c8bceae-a8f8-59df-9913-53898f44b673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485052} :answer-field/id #uuid "16cf85a0-d4e0-503b-a40c-377068739a10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df658338-ffbc-54a4-8fc3-4233fa4b9c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df658338-ffbc-54a4-8fc3-4233fa4b9c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485286} :answer-field/id #uuid "91a5a09a-06e9-5e46-b927-635849a5367f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e847ec-d131-5985-94dc-25f91ed6df64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3e847ec-d131-5985-94dc-25f91ed6df64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485336} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc2e3df9-3029-583e-b5fd-63d9b4b790dc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485478}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4c5958e-629a-595b-ba26-53d736ebe0b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320017" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore,\n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$ gives a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which would require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$ gives a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which requires finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115058 :question/id #uuid "7ab158e6-4222-5cab-88a0-85ce74a7d4b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4413" :question/problem "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\nII. $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\nIII. $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} {:answer/id #uuid "a3967aa3-4b50-5c5c-b5fe-aa477f5fe032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} :answer-field/id #uuid "149d811f-1bfd-59da-848a-31d1c4100def" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86075d40-0e3f-586b-9449-798158d86bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448634} {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cdc4938-08ac-5768-9c3a-6cf1b96bf157" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8546691d-f8b4-5754-96f8-903691eb5eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448636} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc3e7d1-fdc0-5ebf-9944-36f12a7d8eff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449358}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e648555-87e2-52bf-ac70-24ae7f7d32c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42265" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n- **II.** $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n- **III.** $AC+BC=(A+B)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84adee91-f9b3-5089-890e-41b5e257813d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448638} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e31c4f-b7bd-5276-a991-deb172fd1702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e31c4f-b7bd-5276-a991-deb172fd1702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448639} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d1bd3d1-8fdb-5689-a908-f1bc0ac9ac01" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1670a685-9e94-5937-8cfd-7d0d29af6eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448640} {:answer/id #uuid "16ec1bf8-e36a-5bfb-84bd-a4334c07e464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1670a685-9e94-5937-8cfd-7d0d29af6eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448640} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b55508-2a98-5d52-9e53-d6536bd357ec" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113b4e99-4e5b-55aa-a4da-2a14a868af02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448642} {:answer/id #uuid "056450c3-2bbe-583e-950a-5fcae4730b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "113b4e99-4e5b-55aa-a4da-2a14a868af02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448642} :answer-field/id #uuid "96d5b3ee-a8ea-534b-8e66-6ca762d54d43" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449361}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "174631dd-f119-50e8-bf7b-ac669b330d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-42266" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(A+B)C=AC+BC$\n- **II.** $AB=BA$\n- **III.** $A(BC)=(BA)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC)=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5721fddb-4ddb-5ceb-8d53-beb5879aabb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448386} {:answer/id #uuid "94b7a979-8ec2-54e2-90a3-0c1ddb63d731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b7a979-8ec2-54e2-90a3-0c1ddb63d731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448387} :answer-field/id #uuid "808c3874-e879-50ff-9b4f-7080ca2b02ad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f74fb5a-177b-5835-b20e-ce0567027248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448388} {:answer/id #uuid "06d94795-ebf6-5369-a12b-dbfa3c0bde79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f74fb5a-177b-5835-b20e-ce0567027248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448388} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bc69198-ea95-5680-86fb-59feb160bb36" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f629e2cf-0d6b-5ebd-ba20-35e8b11008d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448390} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab0f40e-90eb-52f5-8bf5-16588c5aca46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f629e2cf-0d6b-5ebd-ba20-35e8b11008d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448390} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7d9849-da3b-534a-83ba-7cddee8c3884" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449235}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8250ce52-a1e9-536b-9512-ee968aac3cef" :question/math-academy-id "q-130446" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${A}^{2}B=A(AB)$\n- **II.** $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- **III.** $B(CA)=(CB)A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  ${A}^{2}B=AAB=A(AB)$ is always true.\n\n- Statement II is false.  Matrix multiplication is distributive and  $A(B-C)=AB-AC.$ However, matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AC\\ne CA$ in general and therefore $A(B-C)\\ne AB-CA$, in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $B(CA)=(BC)A.$ However, matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $BC\\ne CB$ in general and therefore $B(CA)\\ne (CB)A$, in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420d6cc9-8195-5ce4-9357-adff9f06e789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449472} {:answer/id #uuid "dfaff5dd-3001-57cc-a214-27e4b2f13a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfaff5dd-3001-57cc-a214-27e4b2f13a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449473} :answer-field/id #uuid "e83edd0f-1ee5-57a0-b8f2-861740202905" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a96d375-e3c1-5d42-b10d-88fedd420645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449474} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d1552b-b0c1-5914-8616-b9aa0f71d996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a96d375-e3c1-5d42-b10d-88fedd420645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449474} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e5d71a8-1832-50ab-a267-82a5ea4c6510" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd4a080-8694-528b-99c0-94bb7afe0160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449476} {:answer/id #uuid "b70ca1e9-55e1-5e83-8b86-ac7385727b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b70ca1e9-55e1-5e83-8b86-ac7385727b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449477} :answer-field/id #uuid "43485488-f54f-56dd-98bd-bbf9a37fb3ae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450692}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a216ad8-b070-56d6-a23a-d32e7322b41f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130449" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $3\\times 3$ matrices, and  ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=A{I}_{3}B$\n- **II.** $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB$\n- **III.** ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $A{I}_{3}B=(A{I}_{3})B=AB.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB+A{I}_{3}=AB+A.$ However,  $AB+A\\ne AB,$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7957644-0d34-5355-b4aa-6843421f4cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449478} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfd816a-e282-554a-bc11-458d1326d8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccfd816a-e282-554a-bc11-458d1326d8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449479} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fcf8fbd-79c9-5a3f-9c93-3269eb1a6b18" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5609b0ad-b55f-5942-bbdd-8d585ee962ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449480} {:answer/id #uuid "8db8304a-b1d0-5052-b18c-e9bb08899b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5609b0ad-b55f-5942-bbdd-8d585ee962ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449480} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b9348d-3f50-5361-9ba1-8262be95c0a0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5099a79-f035-55b7-a74f-976fa8b79237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449482} {:answer/id #uuid "96ca6167-ad12-543c-a1c9-e7474101a124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5099a79-f035-55b7-a74f-976fa8b79237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449482} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd08e90-18cc-5f16-8ac5-f89ed5e9b611" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450695}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da216097-76ab-5a2e-b3ad-662534506edb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130455" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A(BC)=(AB)C$\n\n- **II.** $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n\n- **III.** $CA=AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III  is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $CA\\ne AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3e23a78-9cff-5f4f-b321-68256103a287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449484} {:answer/id #uuid "fc24f783-305e-584a-96dc-56e90c7199d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc24f783-305e-584a-96dc-56e90c7199d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449485} :answer-field/id #uuid "599aa420-34d9-5e48-96d9-1fff3725e551" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd393f3-55f2-599a-aa0a-d18ad1ef34f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449486} {:answer/id #uuid "1566549e-0426-589d-92ea-3d623677f3b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cd393f3-55f2-599a-aa0a-d18ad1ef34f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449486} :answer-field/id #uuid "d184eea5-c9c5-5b93-8586-c6e75fec6d77" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7fff099-59fc-5bf2-850f-508b365824eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449488} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b157f5-5880-5d42-b0af-3314832fb23c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4b157f5-5880-5d42-b0af-3314832fb23c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449489} :answer-field/id #uuid "c228a2f4-4fa2-5cb5-ad55-1810d368d693" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450698}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c886d4f7-2a2b-5730-a24b-3976b9e31d35" :question/math-academy-id "q-130463" :question/problem "Given that $A$ and $B$  are $8\\times 8$ matrices,  and ${I}_{8}$ is the $8\\times 8$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A$\n- **II.** $AB=BA$\n- **III.** $A\\cdot 2{I}_{8}=2A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot 2{I}_{8} & =A({I}_{8}+{I}_{8}) \\\\  & =A{I}_{8}+A{I}_{8} \\\\  & =A+A \\\\  & =2A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statements I  and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f505436-de5e-5e74-9c16-db47f9d3dde8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449490} {:answer/id #uuid "55ad8fd2-983a-52f3-adb4-1610dbb1063d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f505436-de5e-5e74-9c16-db47f9d3dde8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449490} :answer-field/id #uuid "61886434-6b69-5a05-bc4e-5fe067d4aadb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e4cb8a-161c-5b37-8171-e110c0ccabdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449492} {:answer/id #uuid "c53c0d38-c0d6-534c-98d5-3e8b2cf7c4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c53c0d38-c0d6-534c-98d5-3e8b2cf7c4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449493} :answer-field/id #uuid "6517376b-dc67-5612-af55-6316cd92e350" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45243252-dbf8-5dba-81eb-702f3231cb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449494} {:answer/id #uuid "5489dffc-c13b-505b-b7ba-aa63f4669cd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45243252-dbf8-5dba-81eb-702f3231cb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449494} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd0867ba-7318-50a7-adfb-0f8ddb112341" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450701}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca328f5c-fde3-5a0e-88ed-9bc8ff6b0334" :question/math-academy-id "q-130478" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(CA)B=C(BA)$\n- **II.** $(A+A)B=2AB$\n- **III.** $CB=BC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I  is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $(CA)B=C(AB)$ is always true. However,  matrix multiplication is not commutative,   $AB\\ne BA$ in general. Therefore, $(CA)B\\ne C(BA)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+A)B=AB+AB=2AB$ is always true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, so $CB\\ne BC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329640 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98d094e2-1177-5e99-96ad-7caeee897640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450618} {:answer/id #uuid "ca99c815-da6d-51d7-a07d-611d7659f788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98d094e2-1177-5e99-96ad-7caeee897640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450618} :answer-field/id #uuid "c30fd7ce-bd14-59fb-ab10-845f8a59bb92" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956b7a25-6517-5ef2-837c-39c50a5c5a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450620} {:answer/id #uuid "bd63bdd4-4b06-56ad-b67b-a613cc1dd46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd63bdd4-4b06-56ad-b67b-a613cc1dd46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450621} :answer-field/id #uuid "382ec9ba-1720-5328-8c38-f194ab93dcab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451264} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "762ad639-2afc-55e3-bdc7-be4e7057c714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450622} {:answer/id #uuid "7a78eef3-ff9c-56b5-98cb-545a4b324d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "762ad639-2afc-55e3-bdc7-be4e7057c714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450622} :answer-field/id #uuid "800a3551-29f1-5bb8-a3bc-66ca201c01c9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451265}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "005a0156-3d99-59d1-ab99-adf9b9b4c7b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42264" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n\n- **II.** $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n\n- **III.** $A(B-C)=(B-C)A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $A(B-C)\\ne (B-C)A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329641 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ede5fc7-4e98-54a5-a8b6-e3d24c4c38db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450624} {: