n/math-academy-id "q-42267" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $5\\times 5$ matrices, and  ${I}_{5}$ is the $5\\times 5$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n- **II.** $A(B+C)=AB+AC$\n- **III.** $B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B=B.$\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b4b6c9-b120-5669-8778-9d44bd03a705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451627} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9ff174-54f1-5fc0-82c9-56c7f68be83b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9ff174-54f1-5fc0-82c9-56c7f68be83b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451628} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6596886-eb35-5a15-8678-0d03898ac57c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b1b7dcd-0a45-5a31-b1e7-359ba6b8ce48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451629} {:answer/id #uuid "2844641e-66b1-56cc-8371-e36f6a1b3ff0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b7dcd-0a45-5a31-b1e7-359ba6b8ce48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451629} :answer-field/id #uuid "648f05bf-a002-5add-8c9a-e67860f117ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aec13ecc-22bc-5436-b215-dddd0d181f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451631} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfc103f-6039-5ed8-b224-6f15716dcaa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aec13ecc-22bc-5436-b215-dddd0d181f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451631} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce1dbe9-397b-565f-a4c9-e832cb32d032" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452663}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c88851c-8567-55d2-897e-8b0f9b020c35" :question/math-academy-id "q-75662" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A(B+C)=AC+AB$\n- **II.** $A(BC)=(BA)C$\n- **III.** $AB=BA$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\nA(B+C)=AB+AC=AC+AB\n$$\n\n since matrix addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC)=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fd2d4af-fcc8-55b6-bf9b-9feed35a4e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451633} {:answer/id #uuid "8c44c3d1-8408-5b27-9d56-5820850d8e6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fd2d4af-fcc8-55b6-bf9b-9feed35a4e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451633} :answer-field/id #uuid "875098b9-5492-5e1a-b53e-55972f8d78c0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c09b308-44c0-5d82-b117-e79d490fc908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451635} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ea9fe4-7d06-5ee2-81e0-6e343876dfb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ea9fe4-7d06-5ee2-81e0-6e343876dfb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451636} :answer-field/id #uuid "f365105a-7265-5164-bb84-ae009541d7d4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086cedd9-2c5d-5cf5-8342-fff602804217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451637} {:answer/id #uuid "d576ec60-2dbd-5562-90ac-ff700e520b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d576ec60-2dbd-5562-90ac-ff700e520b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451638} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf272d3-96d9-5e52-bf3a-2077d76af75c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452666}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8619c3de-3523-5f87-a248-dac65df502b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-75664" :question/problem "Given that $A$ and $B$  are $4\\times 4$ matrices,  and ${I}_{4}$ is the $4\\times 4$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n- **II.** $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A$\n- **III.** $A(B+{I}_{4})=AB+A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A=A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{4})=AB+A{I}_{4}=AB+A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements II  and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d29adab0-49f5-5be8-9dfb-41b652b9f78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451639} {:answer/id #uuid "aae53705-b1e7-5ad4-a458-fc12bd5715e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d29adab0-49f5-5be8-9dfb-41b652b9f78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ec2f6a3-b7c4-5dbf-b313-e1460364d497" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "163312b5-47ae-51a4-8302-780627f27eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451641} {:answer/id #uuid "8391eb9d-de48-5257-958c-71e626ee3926" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "163312b5-47ae-51a4-8302-780627f27eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451641} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e9e4ab6-972e-5a28-8a06-204e593f15c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5abcda23-f4db-5653-8749-2127e4eb2cc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451643} {:answer/id #uuid "83789ace-8be4-5fa7-bb78-667b324a5f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83789ace-8be4-5fa7-bb78-667b324a5f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451644} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebdef35b-4dc7-5168-954f-85f588629353" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452669}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ca7b9cd-e052-55a9-b9b9-9f438a40909d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75717" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $CB=BC$\n- **II.** $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- **III.** $A(BC)=(AB)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statement  III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0baea8e6-67f2-5e1f-8d1f-49751d15a460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484839} {:answer/id #uuid "150d4133-0a25-50d9-a5b6-3426cedc7ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484857} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bd451c-1d47-509f-8a91-0bb7d9a2e039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485211} {:answer/id #uuid "b779c7a3-5d4b-56ea-9ee5-63a3e5e72954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485212} {:answer/id #uuid "d6de882f-5289-5eb0-83ae-5e40d163532c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0baea8e6-67f2-5e1f-8d1f-49751d15a460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484839} :answer-field/id #uuid "72242043-aa0f-565d-a557-78a4b73b318a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96d290b8-46cc-5702-9916-bb75bce9f305" :question/math-academy-id "q-75663" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, and ${I}_{4}$ is the $4\\times 4$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A$\n\nII. $(CA)B=C(AB)$\n\nIII. $BC=CB$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is asociative, so $(CA)B=C(AB)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $BC\\ne CB$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I  and II are true."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}]}
